# ── talhelper (TALOS-0bo8) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The secrets bundle carries the cluster's IDENTITY: all five CAs (os, k8s, etcd,
# k8s-aggregator, k8s-serviceaccount), the machine token, the k8s bootstrap token,
# the secretbox encryption secret, and cluster.id / cluster.secret. Anyone holding
# it can mint a node into this cluster. It is backed up to 1Password and must NEVER
# be committed — this entry exists so that cannot happen by accident.
# ⚠️ MATCHED BY FILENAME, NOT PATH — deliberately.
#
# These were originally `talos/talsecret.yaml`, an anchored path. The planned migration ends
# with `mv talos/ configs/`, at which point an anchored rule stops matching and a subsequent
# `git add` would stage the cluster's entire CA and token bundle. Verified: with the anchored
# form, `git check-ignore configs/talsecret.yaml` returned nothing.
#
# Filename patterns survive the directory move. Do not re-anchor these.
talsecret.yaml
talsecret.sops.yaml
**/talsecret.yaml
**/talsecret.sops.yaml

# Generated machine configs. Same reason: they embed the bundle's contents inline.
# Regenerate with `talhelper genconfig` rather than tracking them.
# Generated machine configs — they embed the secrets bundle inline. Filename-matched for the
# same reason as above, so the rule survives the directory rename.
clusterconfig/
**/clusterconfig/
